  "awb---how-to-step-2-des": "A subhead such as for operations leads at companies with one warehouse sorts the room before anyone registers. Below it, list the sessions or acts with start times. A conference needs the full agenda; a party needs one line about the night.",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Event Page Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an event landing page?\", \"a\": \"An event landing page is a single page built to get people to one event, such as a conference or a launch party. It gives the date and the venue, makes the case for coming and takes registrations through one form.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I build a landing page for an event?\", \"a\": \"Decide what each registrant has to tell you, then write down the date and the venue. With Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, you describe the event in a prompt. Emergent builds the page and the registration form, plus the guest list table behind them.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are good event landing page examples?\", \"a\": \"Unbounce and OptimizePress both publish roundups of event landing page examples. Dribbble collects event layouts under its own tag. Across the best event landing pages, the same pattern repeats: date and venue in the first screen, one form, real photos of the room.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are there free event landing page templates?\", \"a\": \"Design galleries and builder marketplaces offer free event landing page templates. A template gives you the layout, while the guest list and the confirmation emails still need setting up. Emergent's free tier covers building and publishing the page with those pieces included.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do the best event landing pages include that others leave out?\", \"a\": \"Answers to what guests would otherwise email about: the ticket price, parking or transit, whether food is served, and the refund policy. The best event landing pages place each answer near the form. Accessibility details, such as step-free entry, belong there too.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an event registration landing page include?\", \"a\": \"It needs the date and the venue, then a form short enough to finish on a phone. After submit, a thank you page confirms the place and repeats the address. The registrant should leave with everything needed to arrive on time.\"}, {\"q\": \"What goes on a conference landing page?\", \"a\": \"A conference needs more than most events: the agenda by day and track, speaker photos with one line each, the venue with nearby hotels and the registration types. The strongest conference landing page examples keep the form one click from every section.\"}, {\"q\": \"How is a virtual event landing page different?\", \"a\": \"A virtual event has no venue. The page trades the address and directions for a join link and a start time in each visitor's own zone. For a single online session, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/webinar-landing-page'>webinar landing page</a> is the closer fit.\"}, {\"q\": \"What makes good event landing page design?\", \"a\": \"Good event landing page design puts the date and the register button in the first screen on a phone. Use one real photo of the venue or a past crowd instead of stock. Repeat the button after the agenda for visitors who read to the end.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is it better to build separate event landing pages for each date?\", \"a\": \"Only when the dates differ in audience, price, or program. A roadshow repeating one agenda in several cities works on a single page with a city picker on the form. A venue or club with a monthly calendar needs one events landing page listing every date, each linking to its own registration page.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}